Hi all,

I am developping a R package on github. It now is version 1.0, previous version was 0.1.

I deployed a Shiny app on shinyapps.io <http://shinyapps.io> using version 0.1. Then I updated the package and now want the app to work with version 1.0. I have tried deleting the app, changing package name, etc., but it still works with the old version. I know it because the new version should support a given type of file input that gives an error with the app, which it wouldn't if the right package version were installed.

Has anyone experienced similar issues? How to update an app dependency?

Thanks a lot, best wishes

Maëlle.

